    "source_answer": "\\[60^\\circ \\]",
    "previous_model_response": "The triangle is right-angled, with respect to \\(\\theta\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{opposite}=12,\\qquad \\text{adjacent}=8\\sqrt3.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\tan\\theta=\\frac{12}{8\\sqrt3}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\approx 40.9^\\circ.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{40.9^\\circ}\n\\]"
  },
  "answer_verification": {
    "status": "verified",
    "verified_answer": "60 degrees",
    "reasoning": "In the right triangle the hypotenuse is 8 sqrt(3) and the leg opposite theta is 12, so sin(theta)=12/(8 sqrt(3))=sqrt(3)/2, hence theta=60 degrees."
  }
